# Backend conventions

- Feature modules, not layer modules: `trips/`, `rigs/`, `conditions/`, `calibration/`,
  `charter/`, `billing/`. Each owns its controller, service, DTOs, and tests.
- Controllers do routing and validation only. All logic in services. No Prisma calls in
  controllers.
- Every external API integration lives in `apps/api/src/integrations/<source>/` behind an
  interface, with a recorded-fixture test. Never call an external API from a service
  directly.
- BullMQ queues: `bundles` (region prefetch generation), `ingest` (external data pulls),
  `calibration` (probe fit jobs), `notify`. Queue names are constants in
  `apps/api/src/queues/names.ts`. Every job is idempotent and safe to retry.
- Cache external data in Redis with an explicit TTL matched to the source's real update
  cadence (see `docs/04-data-sources.md`). Never cache indefinitely, never re-fetch a
  static tide table hourly.
- Rate-limit every outbound integration. NOAA and ADF&G endpoints are public goods; be a
  good citizen and back off on 429/5xx with jitter.
- Auth: JWT access + refresh, org-scoped. Every query that touches user data goes through
  a scoping helper — never trust a client-supplied `orgId` or `userId`.
- Money is integer cents. Stripe webhooks are verified and idempotent by event id.
